      "title": "Coolant Crossover Pipe and Thermostat Housing Leak",
      "description": "The Catera 3.0L V6 coolant crossover pipe and plastic thermostat housing develop cracks and leaks. The plastic components become brittle with heat cycling and fail, causing coolant loss and overheating that can warp the aluminum cylinder heads.",
      "solution": "Replace the thermostat housing and coolant crossover pipe. Upgrade to aluminum aftermarket components if available. Replace the thermostat at the same time. Flush the cooling system with fresh coolant.",
